  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Alice is given a binary string SSS of length NNN.\n\nShe can perform the following operations on string SSS:\n\n\nSelect an index 1≤i≤∣S∣1\\le i\\le |S|1≤i≤∣S∣ and delete the character SiS_iSi​.;\nSelect an index 1≤i≤∣S∣1\\le i\\le |S|1≤i≤∣S∣ and flip the character SiS_iSi​. Note that while flipping 111 becomes 000 and vice-versa.\nFind the **lexicographically smallest** string Alice can obtain using **at most** KKK operations.\n\nNote that string XXX is said to be lexicographically smaller than string YYY if:\n\n\nString XXX is a prefix of string YYY, or;\nThe smallest index iii where XXX and YYY differ, Xi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — denoting length of the string and the maximum number of operations, respectively.\nThe next line contains a binary string SSS of length NNN.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **lexicographically smallest** string that Alice can make.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤K&lt;N0 \\leq K \\lt N0≤K&lt;N",
      "SSS is a Binary String",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
